This repository builds on, uses or measures the following third-party work.

Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B model weights
  PrismML, https://huggingface.co/prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-gguf (Apache-2.0).
  Not redistributed here; scripts/fetch_model.py downloads them from PrismML at a pinned revision.
  The base model is Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B. The PTQ1_0 format, the PrismML llama.cpp fork and the
  baseline measured in docs/ladder.md are PrismML's work.

PrismML llama.cpp fork
  https://github.com/PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp, commit 6067dbea986ed1359db98c42ab06eb49426bbf16 (MIT),
  derived from ggml-org/llama.cpp (MIT, Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors).
  Fetched at build time and linked for tokenization and the chat template; its vendored
  nlohmann/json (MIT) header is used by the engine. The code views in docs/steps/ are excerpts of
  this fork and of modifications to it.
  The beam-selection drafter option in engine/src/draft.cu follows PrismML llama.cpp #284
  (opt-in; disabled in the measured profiles).

GSM8K
  Cobbe et al., "Training Verifiers to Solve Math Word Problems" (2021),
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/openai/gsm8k (MIT, Copyright (c) 2021 OpenAI).
  data/video-gsm-prompts256.bin contains GSM8K test questions with an appended answer-format
  instruction. receipts/gsm8k/ contains model outputs on the GSM8K test set.

Math-Verify (Hugging Face, Apache-2.0) is used for GSM8K answer scoring.

Additional engine and research exports (October 2026)
  engines/NOTICE and component LICENSE/NOTICE files preserve engine/vendor attributions.
  benchmarks/NOTICE and benchmarks/README.md describe benchmark dependencies and dataset custody.
  research/ preserves our binary/packed kernel source, finite proofs and selected technical evidence;
  component notices and upstream attributions apply to code derived from those dependencies.
  These exports do not redistribute model weights or grant rights beyond each upstream license.
